    "narrative": "For September 10, **Bryce Harper** (74.25) stands as our premier offensive anchor, benefitting from a favorable matchup against Javier (xERA 4.49) and a prime spot in the three-hole. While **Luis Arraez** (64.63) and **Justin Crawford** (63.80) are also strong starts against the same pitcher, **Bryce Harper**\u2019s superior xwOBA metrics and favorable park factors make him our most reliable asset for run production today. **Justin Crawford** remains particularly vital to our strategy; despite hitting lower in the order, his speed profile provides essential coverage in the scarcest category, SB, justifying his start even against the volatility of a mid-tier arm.\n\nThe rotation decisions today were dictated by a cautious approach to game caps. **Braden Montgomery** (39.60) was the most difficult exclusion, falling just shy of our 40.0 efficiency floor due to a marginal matchup against Jones (xERA 3.57). While **Braden Montgomery**\u2019s switch-hitting ability and recent form were considered, his lack of an elite platoon edge kept him on the bench. Conversely, **Daulton Varsho** (50.29) makes the cut as a fringe start; while he faces the formidable Wheeler (xERA 3.24), his dynamic platoon advantage against a right-hander effectively neutralized the pitcher's skill penalty, keeping him safely above the floor.\n\nSeveral rostered players, including **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Lawrence Butler**, are unavailable today due to schedule gaps, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active corps. We are monitoring **Cal Raleigh** (43.49) closely; while he is in the lineup against the elite deGrom, his efficiency score is suppressed by the high caliber of the opposing starter. We advise keeping an eye on late-breaking weather or lineup changes for **Cal Raleigh**, **Kyle Karros**, and the rest of the squad, as any degradation in those conditions would risk pushing these marginal starts below our acceptable risk threshold.",
